<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>
  <!--
    The turbocharger (Framework 0.320.0; docs/development/vehicle-turbocharger.md; the owner's cards of 26 Nov 2026: "modelled like the rest
    of the components, and with the rest of the components"). A part of its own (Turbochargers.cs appends it to every design with a piston
    engine) and this system, which runs only while the vehicle has a turbocharger: built in (the engine's Def says turbocharged) or fitted
    (the turbocharger fitting grants Turbocharger). The lubrication system brings it with it (comesWith), so every piston loadout has it.
    Not yet tested in game.

    Sources and labels:
    - A turbocharger's shaft runs on plain bearings fed by the engine's own oil; oil starvation is the commonest cause of turbocharger
      failure, and stopping a hot engine at once cooks the oil left in the bearing housing ("coking"). Secondary: turbocharger makers'
      service literature as commonly cited (Garrett's and Holset's failure guides; no figure checked). Every rate below is authored.
    - Dust past a clogged or leaking air filter erodes the compressor wheel's blades. Secondary, the same literature; rates authored.
    - Boost builds with engine speed and load (turbo lag at low speed): the curves are authored, shaped like a typical diesel's.
    - Wear on boost: about 2,500 hours at full boost to wear a standard-boost turbo out (authored; a road turbo lasts roughly the engine's
      life between overhauls). Low boost half that wear, high boost three times it.
    - A worn turbo passes oil past its seals (blue smoke, oil burned); one that fails takes back what it added: the fitting's power
      (x0.83 cancels its x1.2), or for an engine turbocharged as built about 0.7 of its rated power, a naturally aspirated engine's share
      (authored; turbocharging commonly adds a third or more to a diesel's output). The thin-air hold goes with it (Powertrain.AirPowerShare).
    - A turbo that fails with the engine running can send pieces of its compressor wheel into the engine: 15% of the engine's health, once
      (authored), behind the "a failing turbocharger can damage the engine" setting (on).
    Its health is the part's own: hits, fire and blasts wear it like any part, and a destroyed one is replaced from the turbocharger repair
    supply (PartSupplies.xml).
  -->
  <Phobos.VehicleSystems.PhobosVehicleSystemDef>
    <defName>PhobosVehicleSystem_Turbocharger</defName>
    <label>turbocharger</label>
    <description>The turbocharger: exhaust gas spins a compressor that forces more air into the engine. It runs on the engine's oil, so low oil wears it fast; dust past a clogged air filter, high boost and stopping the engine while it is hot wear it too. A worn one smokes, burns oil and loses boost; one that fails can take a piece out of the engine.</description>
    <needsGrant>Turbocharger</needsGrant>
    <roles>
      <li>Turbocharger</li>
      <li>Engine</li>
    </roles>
    <parameters>
      <!-- How fast the turbocharger's heat follows the engine's load, a share of the gap an hour (authored: it settles in about ten game
           minutes, so a short idle cools it). -->
      <turboHeatRate>6</turboHeatRate>
    </parameters>
    <quantities>
      <li>
        <name>turboBoost</name>
        <label>boost</label>
        <description>How hard the turbocharger is pushing air into the engine, as a share of its full boost. It builds with engine speed and load, and a worn turbocharger gives less.</description>
        <unit>Fraction</unit>
        <derivedFrom>
          <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Input_PartEfficiency">
            <role>Turbocharger</role>
            <missing>0</missing>
          </li>
          <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Input_EngineRunning" />
          <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Input_EngineRpm">
            <!-- Turbo lag: little boost at idle, full boost from mid revs (authored). -->
            <curve>
              <points>
                <li>(0, 0.05)</li>
                <li>(800, 0.05)</li>
                <li>(1300, 0.5)</li>
                <li>(1700, 1)</li>
                <li>(8000, 1)</li>
              </points>
            </curve>
          </li>
          <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Input_EngineLoad">
            <curve>
              <points>
                <li>(0, 0.1)</li>
                <li>(1, 1)</li>
              </points>
            </curve>
          </li>
        </derivedFrom>
        <stages>
          <li>
            <!-- Wear on boost, by the boost tune (authored): standard about 2,500 hours at full boost to wear it out, low half that, high three
                 times it. -->
            <from>0.6</from>
            <label>on boost</label>
            <effects>
              <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Effect_DamagePart">
                <role>Turbocharger</role>
                <sharePerHour>0.0002</sharePerHour>
                <when Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.When_Tune">
                  <tune>PhobosTune_BoostLow</tune>
                </when>
              </li>
              <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Effect_DamagePart">
                <role>Turbocharger</role>
                <sharePerHour>0.0004</sharePerHour>
                <when Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.When_Tune">
                  <tune>PhobosTune_BoostStandard</tune>
                </when>
              </li>
              <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Effect_DamagePart">
                <role>Turbocharger</role>
                <sharePerHour>0.0012</sharePerHour>
                <when Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.When_Tune">
                  <tune>PhobosTune_BoostHigh</tune>
                </when>
              </li>
            </effects>
          </li>
        </stages>
      </li>
      <li>
        <name>turboCondition</name>
        <label>turbocharger</label>
        <description>What is left of the turbocharger. Worn, it smokes blue, burns oil and gives less boost; failed, the engine loses what the turbo gave it and holds no power in thin air.</description>
        <unit>Fraction</unit>
        <derivedFrom>
          <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Input_PartHealth">
            <role>Turbocharger</role>
          </li>
        </derivedFrom>
        <stages>
          <li>
            <to>0.001</to>
            <label>failed</label>
            <notable>true</notable>
            <effects>
              <!-- A fitted turbo gives back its x1.2 (x0.83); an engine turbocharged as built drops to about a naturally aspirated one's
                   share (authored). -->
              <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Effect_EnginePower">
                <factor>0.83</factor>
                <when Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.When_FittingGrants">
                  <ability>Turbocharger</ability>
                </when>
              </li>
              <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Effect_EnginePower">
                <factor>0.7</factor>
                <when Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.When_TurbochargedAsBuilt" />
              </li>
              <!-- Pieces of the compressor wheel into a running engine, once as it fails (authored), behind its setting. -->
              <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Effect_DamagePart">
                <role>Engine</role>
                <share>0.15</share>
                <when Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.When_All">
                  <conditions>
                    <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.When_EngineRunning" />
                    <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.When_Setting">
                      <setting>turboFailureDamagesEngine</setting>
                    </li>
                  </conditions>
                </when>
              </li>
              <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Effect_RateQuantity">
                <quantity>oilLevel</quantity>
                <perHour>-0.01</perHour>
                <when Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.When_EngineRunning" />
              </li>
              <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Effect_Fleck">
                <fleck>Smoke</fleck>
                <perHour>40</perHour>
                <scale>0.9</scale>
                <when Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.When_EngineRunning" />
              </li>
              <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Effect_Message">
                <message>PhobosVehicleSystems_MsgTurboFailed</message>
              </li>
            </effects>
          </li>
          <li>
            <from>0.001</from>
            <to>0.2</to>
            <label>failing</label>
            <notable>true</notable>
            <effects>
              <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Effect_EnginePower">
                <factor>0.92</factor>
              </li>
              <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Effect_RateQuantity">
                <quantity>oilLevel</quantity>
                <perHour>-0.004</perHour>
                <when Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.When_EngineRunning" />
              </li>
              <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Effect_Fleck">
                <fleck>Smoke</fleck>
                <perHour>20</perHour>
                <scale>0.7</scale>
                <when Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.When_EngineRunning" />
              </li>
              <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Effect_Message">
                <message>PhobosVehicleSystems_MsgTurboFailing</message>
                <type>CautionInput</type>
              </li>
            </effects>
          </li>
          <li>
            <from>0.2</from>
            <to>0.5</to>
            <label>worn</label>
            <notable>true</notable>
            <effects>
              <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Effect_EnginePower">
                <factor>0.97</factor>
              </li>
              <!-- Oil past worn seals: as much again as the engine's own burn (Systems_Lubrication.xml's 0.15% an hour, authored). -->
              <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Effect_RateQuantity">
                <quantity>oilLevel</quantity>
                <perHour>-0.0015</perHour>
                <when Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.When_EngineRunning" />
              </li>
              <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Effect_Fleck">
                <fleck>Smoke</fleck>
                <perHour>8</perHour>
                <scale>0.5</scale>
                <when Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.When_EngineRunning" />
              </li>
              <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Effect_Message">
                <message>PhobosVehicleSystems_MsgTurboWorn</message>
                <type>CautionInput</type>
              </li>
            </effects>
          </li>
        </stages>
      </li>
      <li>
        <name>turboOilFeed</name>
        <label>turbo oil feed</label>
        <description>Oil reaching the turbocharger's bearings, from the engine's oil pump. Low oil or a weak pump starves them and wears the turbocharger fast.</description>
        <unit>Fraction</unit>
        <hidden>true</hidden>
        <derivedFrom>
          <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Input_Quantity">
            <quantity>oilPressure</quantity>
            <fallback Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Input_Constant">
              <value>1</value>
            </fallback>
          </li>
        </derivedFrom>
        <stages>
          <li>
            <!-- Nothing reaching the bearings: about two running hours to ruin it, faster than the engine's own five (authored). -->
            <to>0.15</to>
            <label>dry</label>
            <notable>true</notable>
            <effects>
              <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Effect_DamagePart">
                <role>Turbocharger</role>
                <sharePerHour>0.5</sharePerHour>
                <when Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.When_EngineRunning" />
              </li>
            </effects>
          </li>
          <li>
            <!-- Low oil: about twenty running hours (authored). An idling engine on a half-empty sump reads here. -->
            <from>0.15</from>
            <to>0.5</to>
            <label>starved</label>
            <notable>true</notable>
            <effects>
              <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Effect_DamagePart">
                <role>Turbocharger</role>
                <sharePerHour>0.05</sharePerHour>
                <when Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.When_EngineRunning" />
              </li>
            </effects>
          </li>
        </stages>
      </li>
      <li>
        <name>turboGrit</name>
        <label>grit in the intake</label>
        <description>Dust getting past a clogged air filter into the compressor, worse in deserts and sandstorms. It erodes the turbocharger's blades; an engine service fits a clean filter.</description>
        <unit>Plain</unit>
        <!-- The dust factor reaches 12 in a desert sandstorm (DustRule), so the reading may too. -->
        <max>12</max>
        <hidden>true</hidden>
        <derivedFrom>
          <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Input_Quantity">
            <quantity>airFilter</quantity>
            <!-- Only a filter past clogged lets grit by (the service system's clogged stage starts at 0.7). -->
            <curve>
              <points>
                <li>(0, 0)</li>
                <li>(0.7, 0)</li>
                <li>(1, 1)</li>
              </points>
            </curve>
            <fallback Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Input_Constant">
              <value>0</value>
            </fallback>
          </li>
          <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Input_Dust" />
          <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Input_EngineRunning" />
        </derivedFrom>
        <stages>
          <li>
            <!-- About a hundred running hours to ruin it (authored). -->
            <from>0.3</from>
            <to>1</to>
            <label>dusty</label>
            <notable>true</notable>
            <effects>
              <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Effect_DamagePart">
                <role>Turbocharger</role>
                <sharePerHour>0.01</sharePerHour>
              </li>
            </effects>
          </li>
          <li>
            <!-- A clogged filter in a desert or a sandstorm: about twenty running hours (authored). -->
            <from>1</from>
            <label>sandblasted</label>
            <notable>true</notable>
            <effects>
              <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Effect_DamagePart">
                <role>Turbocharger</role>
                <sharePerHour>0.05</sharePerHour>
              </li>
            </effects>
          </li>
        </stages>
      </li>
      <li>
        <name>turboHeat</name>
        <label>turbo heat</label>
        <description>How hot the turbocharger runs, following the engine's load. Stopping the engine while it is hot cooks the oil in its bearings and wears it: let the engine idle a little before switching off.</description>
        <unit>Fraction</unit>
        <min>0</min>
        <max>1</max>
        <startsAt>Empty</startsAt>
        <stages>
          <li>
            <from>0.6</from>
            <label>hot</label>
            <notable>true</notable>
          </li>
        </stages>
      </li>
    </quantities>
    <flows>
      <li>
        <name>turboHeating</name>
        <quantity>turboHeat</quantity>
        <kind>Toward</kind>
        <target Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Input_EngineLoad" />
        <factorParameter>turboHeatRate</factorParameter>
      </li>
    </flows>
    <onEvents>
      <li>
        <!-- A hot shutdown: 1% of the turbocharger's health each time the engine is switched off hot (authored). -->
        <eventDef>IgnitionOff</eventDef>
        <effects>
          <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Effect_DamagePart">
            <role>Turbocharger</role>
            <share>0.01</share>
            <when Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.When_QuantityAbove">
              <quantity>turboHeat</quantity>
              <value>0.6</value>
            </when>
          </li>
        </effects>
      </li>
    </onEvents>
  </Phobos.VehicleSystems.PhobosVehicleSystemDef>
</Defs>
